    summary: 'SIMD instructions operate on a vector register holding many lanes at once: AVX2 uses 256-bit registers (8 × FP32), AVX-512 uses 512-bit registers (16 × FP32) and ARM offers NEON (128-bit) and SVE. Intel AMX adds tile registers and tile matrix-multiply instructions for BF16 and INT8 that reach several TFLOPS per socket. On an LLM host the CPU still does real ML arithmetic: tokenization and detokenization, embedding lookups, small models and rerankers, sampling and logit processing, and CPU-offloaded or CPU-only inference of quantized models.',
