    summary: 'A multi-socket server is several memory systems joined by a coherent interconnect. Memory attached to the local socket is fastest; memory on the other socket costs an extra hop of roughly 50-100 ns and less bandwidth. GPUs and NICs are attached to a specific socket’s PCIe lanes, so a CPU thread that feeds a GPU from the wrong socket pays the interconnect twice: once for the memory and once for the DMA path.',
